---
import ProseLayout from "../layouts/ProseLayout.astro";
import { app, contactEmail } from "../config";

const mail = `mailto:${contactEmail}`;
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Support"
  description={`Help with ${app.name}: installing, updating, privacy and how to get in touch.`}
>
  <p class="card">
    Need help, found a bug or have an idea? Email
    <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>How do I install {app.name}?</dt>
    <dd>
      Open the <a href="/download">download page</a> on your Android phone, tap
      Download APK and follow the four steps there.
    </dd>

    <dt>Is {app.name} free?</dt>
    <dd>Yes. No watermark on exports, no ads and no account.</dd>

    <dt>Why isn't it on Google Play?</dt>
    <dd>
      {app.name} isn't on Google Play yet. Until it is, this website is the
      place to get it.
    </dd>

    <dt>
      Android warned me about the file, or Play Protect wants to check it. Is
      that normal?
    </dt>
    <dd>
      Yes. Android does that for apps installed from outside Google Play. To
      make sure your copy is the official one, compare it with the fingerprints
      under "Check that the file is genuine" on the{" "}
      <a href="/download">download page</a>.
    </dd>

    <dt>Which phones does it work on?</dt>
    <dd>Android phones running Android {app.minAndroid} or newer.</dd>

    <dt>Is there an iPhone version?</dt>
    <dd>Not yet. {app.name} is on Android for now.</dd>

    <dt>How do I update?</dt>
    <dd>
      Download the new version from the <a href="/download">download page</a>{" "}
      and install it over the old one. Your projects stay.
    </dd>

    <dt>Does {app.name} upload my videos?</dt>
    <dd>
      No. Your videos, photos and projects stay on your phone. Optional cloud AI
      features send only the sound, and only after you agree each time. See the{" "}
      <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </dd>

    <dt>{app.name} closed unexpectedly. How do I report it?</dt>
    <dd>
      Open <strong>Settings → Crash reports</strong>, tap Share and send the
      report to
      <a href={mail}>{contactEmail}</a>, with a line about what you were doing.
    </dd>

    <dt>How do I delete my data?</dt>
    <dd>
      See <a href="/delete-data">Delete your data</a>.
    </dd>
  </dl>
</ProseLayout>
